description: Docker Compose commands must use fixed project name mediajira-v2; never edit compose files.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Docker commands (always)

**Always use `-p mediajira-v2`** with every `docker compose` command in this repo.

```bash
# Correct pattern (always):
docker compose -p mediajira-v2 -f docker-compose.dev.yml <command>

# Examples:
docker compose -p mediajira-v2 -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d --build frontend backend
docker compose -p mediajira-v2 -f docker-compose.dev.yml restart nginx
docker compose -p mediajira-v2 -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec backend python manage.py test
docker compose -p mediajira-v2 -f docker-compose.dev.yml exec backend python manage.py migrate
```

**Never omit `-p mediajira-v2`** — it prevents Docker from generating random container IDs that cause "No such container" and name conflicts during rebuilds.

**Never modify any `docker-compose*.yml` file** (including `docker-compose.dev.yml`). For Docker issues, only run commands or tell the user what to run manually.
